o  update our viewers that we are actually  at 209 versus 112 right now that's 209  for biden and 112  for trump anna heading back to you can  you tell us a little bit about  what we're seeing this evening and some  questions that we might have  uh heading into tomorrow morning if  people start to go to bed soon about  how this election is shaking out in  these key battleground states  well it's definitely looking like it's  not going to be a landslide and that's  one of the things that we were  looking at to see if you know joe biden  pulled ahead by a lot then we could go  to bed  kind of knowing what the result was not  really staying up for the  north carolina and pennsylvania you have  to count every single absentee and mail  and ballot but  it looks like we could really be coming  down to the wire in some of the swing  states  and that means that we could wake up  tomorrow and not know who was won  and of course we have the president  saying that he could come out  and you know declare himself the winner  when it looks like he has  enough support to do so and that might  be before are the results are counted so  you know just under to our watchers and  to our followers  if this is a vote that could uh you know  legally by all the rules set out by all  the states  go forward  and anna what's the likelihood of a red  barrage situation here  where like you mentioned a lot of states  didn't start counting  their early uh mail-in ballots until  today  and maybe people who voted in person  just happen to go more for trump is  there any chance of there being  a perception of trump doing better than  he actually is tonight  well i mean it's certainly true that you  know different  um the different parties have tendencies  of when their voters tend to  cast more votes but it's interesting to  look at a state like atlanta where you  have  you know most of the vote already  counted but the counties  that have not yet been counted are  more around the atlanta era which the  biden campaign is counting on  to go more strongly for them and that's  also the  state where we're seeing two senate  races so  you know we have um a democratic  challenger  john ossoff who's trying to uh unseat  republican  david perdue saying don't make any  declarations yet we're still waiting on  all these atlanta area votes to come in  and it could end up  flipping the race late into the night or  even into tomorrow and the next day  you mentioned these key senate races in  georgia i'm curious  what are some other down the ballot  races that you've been watching this  evening that are  key turning points in this election yeah  well we  and others have already called the house  of representatives for the  democrats that was no real surprise they  had a pretty strong majority going into  this and they were expected to  uh even pick up some seats this in this  election  we're definitely watching a bunch of  senate races  there are 14 races that were considered  competitive and  republicans were defending 12 of them so  one  uh seat that the republicans did pick up  was in alabama  uh incumbent democrat doug jones lost  his alabama senate seat  to a republican so we're gonna see how  the rest of the  night shakes out for the democratic  challengers happening to unseat all the  republicans  you know we're really looking at states  like north carolina where  cal cunningham is a democratic  challenger coming down to the wire  on whether or not he can unseat  republican incumbent  tom tillis and looking at the numbers  right now  uh why should folks who are hoping for a  biden win  uh be either concerned or hopeful about  these numbers  um what are what are the next kind of  big state announcements that people  should have their eyes peeled for  well definitely concerned because it's  not a  biden landslide i mean this is not a  comfortable night for the biden campaign  by any stretch of the imagination it is  going to come down to the wire  and you know we're looking at states  like arizona pennsylvania michigan  wisconsin  you know any configuration of those  states coming together  could mean an electoral college victory  for trump  or for biden and you know that's really  kind of the maddening thing about  the american system is that you you have  uh states that have different rules and  those states are worth different numbers  of electoral college votes  and it just takes a while for that  puzzle to come together and to get a  clear  picture of where we are at this point in  the night  and have you heard anything from folks  within the biden or trump campaigns  about  what needs to happen for either of them  to declare victory tonight  well biden himself said earlier today  that he's willing to wait until tomorrow  if there's nothing to be said he said  he's not going to  come out and just make some kind of  statement tonight just  for the sake of making a statement or  risk getting ahead of himself for the  results  um trump on the other hand is going to  take any opportunity that it looks like  he's ahead enough to declare himself the  way

